{
  "dom_id": "step-119188",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "A **regular polygon** is a polygon where all sides are congruent (have the same length), and all interior angles are congruent (have the same measure).\n\nSome examples of regular polygons are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/d33f23d3d3e301e336d7f70f37e88eee0f605c31b098969805d7c6346e34470e.png)\n\nSome examples of polygons that are **NOT** regular are as follows:\n\n- The rectangle below is **NOT** regular since the sides are not all congruent.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/6d0c6eaee1ae1932d3bd44013c0b8aca977cbe0d98242d5c10aaa24d4f281a77.png)\n\n- The rhombus below is **NOT** regular since the interior angles are not all congruent.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/ce2b908945db56934f08dc0da47f6c708f5220bce3a80f5147362c8b915c5613.png)\n\n- A $30^\\circ$-$60^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle is **NOT** regular since neither the sides nor the angles are all congruent.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/bfe00eb1d1374252fd12f6c74eff7c052021a7305ce10027efc8869f561e3ef5.png)",
